      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — adding a helper assertion method, an `ALL_BITS_SET` constant, inline array literals, and clearer section comments.Now I'll compile-check the file.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored `BinaryCodecTest_testEncodeByteArray.java` introduces an `assertEncodes` helper to eliminate the repetitive encode-and-compare pattern, adds an `ALL_BITS_SET` constant to replace the verbose 8-bit OR expression, uses inline array literals for conciseness, and organizes the 27 assertions into three clearly commented sections (single-byte, two-byte with zero high byte, two-byte with all-set low byte)."
